                        {
                          "metadata": {
                            "name": "PredictCategory"
                          },
                          "outcomes": {
                            "success": "1766017522243"
                          },
                          "code": "PREDICTCATEGORY",
                          "id": "1765977536640",
                          "inputs": [
                            {
                              "id": "1765977536644_1",
                              "name": "prompt",
                              "type": "string",
                              "value": "You are an automated attachment classification agent in a production workflow.\n\nYour task is to classify a single attachment into one of the provided categories using the available metadata and extracted text.\n\nThe extracted text may be incomplete, unstructured, truncated, or noisy due to OCR errors.\n\nYou must follow all instructions exactly.\n\n---\n\n## Input Fields\n\nYou will receive the following inputs:\n\n* Attachment name: Filename of the attachment\n* Attachment type: File type (e.g., pdf, image, docx)\n* Extracted text: Partial or full OCR output (may contain errors)\n* Allowed categories: A fixed list of valid categories (always includes \"Miscellaneous\")\n\n---\n\n## Classification Rules\n\n1. Select exactly one category from the allowed categories.\n2. Do not create, infer, or rename categories.\n3. OCR noise (misspellings, broken words, incorrect characters) is expected and must be tolerated.\n4. Base your decision on:\n\n   * Common document patterns and structure\n   * Keywords and semantic meaning\n   * Filename clues\n   * Formatting indicators (headers, totals, dates, signatures, etc.)\n5. If the content is ambiguous, incomplete, or insufficient for confident classification, select \"Miscellaneous\".\n6. Do not use external knowledge or assumptions beyond the provided input.\n7. The output must be deterministic and reproducible for the same input.\n\n---\n\n## Output Requirements\n\n* Return JSON only.\n* Do not include markdown, explanations outside JSON, or additional fields.\n* The `reason` must be short, factual, and based only on observed evidence.\n\n---\n\n## Output Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"category\": \"string\",\n  \"reason\": \"short explanation\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## User Prompt (Runtime Input)\n\nAttachment name:\n {{$context.$nodes.PROCESSEACHMESSAGE.PROCESSEMAILATTACHMENTS.$currentItem.fileName}} \n\nAttachment type:\n {{$context.$nodes.PROCESSEACHMESSAGE.PROCESSEMAILATTACHMENTS.$currentItem.mimeType}} \n\nExtracted text (partial, may be noisy or incomplete):\n {{$context.$nodes.PROCESSEACHMESSAGE.PROCESSEMAILATTACHMENTS.GETOUTPUTTEXT.$output.result}} \n\nAllowed categories (always includes \"Miscellaneous\"):\n {{$context.$nodes.PROCESSEACHMESSAGE.$currentItem.eligibleCategoryUserNamesList}} \n\n\n---\n\nExample 1\n\nAttachment name:\nJohn_Doe_Resume.pdf\n\nAttachment type:\npdf\n\nExtracted text:\n\nJohn Doe\nSoftware Engineer\nExperience\nJava Python AWS\nEducation\nB.Tech Computer Science\n\nAllowed categories:\n\nResume\n\nCover Letter\n\nInvoice\n\nMiscellaneous\n\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n  \"category\": \"Resume\",\n  \"reason\": \"Contains skills, experience, and education typical of a resume\"\n}\n\n\n---\n\nExample 2 (Noisy OCR)\n\nAttachment name:\nIMG_20240112_093011.jpg\n\nAttachment type:\nimage\n\nExtracted text:\n\nTotai Am0unt : $1,248.76\nDatc 01/12/24\nVisa **** 2391\nThnk you f0r y0ur purchase\n\nAllowed categories:\n\nInvoice\n\nReceipt\n\nBank Statement\n\nMiscellaneous\n\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n  \"category\": \"Receipt\",\n  \"reason\": \"Shows total amount, date, and payment confirmation despite OCR noise\"\n}\n\n---"
                            }
                          ],
                          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"category\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"reason\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
                          "type": "LLM",
                          "convergenceTargetId": "1766018026178"
                        },
